# Android / Gradle

## Versions
- Pin versions in the version catalog (`libs.versions.toml`) or a single root versions block.
- Do not hardcode plugin/dependency versions scattered across modules.

## Deps
- Isolate app vs library modules; avoid circular module deps.
- Prefer official AndroidX / Google artifacts; no mystery AARs without KB note.

## Build hygiene
- Keep `minSdk`/`targetSdk` aligned with project KB; do not bump casually.
- Secrets only via local `local.properties` / CI secrets — never in `build.gradle*`.
- After Gradle edits: sync + assembleDebug (or project smoke) before claiming done.
